    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change enriches the create audit line to include `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping the fields it already logged.\n\nI made a single, small edit to one function \u2014 `onCreate` in `OwnerAuditListener` (a class whose only method is `onCreate`, so `WMC_other` is minimal):\n\n- Added an import for the existing `Membership` utility.\n- Derived `membershipNumber` inline using the same rule the DTO mapper uses (`customerCode + \"-M\" + yy`, null-guarded on `customerCode`/`registrationDate`).\n- Computed `membershipLevel` via `Membership.level(Membership.points(owner, false, false))`, matching the mapper's default derivation.\n- Extended the existing `AUDIT.info(...)` line with the two new placeholders/arguments.\n\nNo new classes or methods were added, and no other file was touched, keeping structural impact to a single simple function in a one-method class. Verified output: `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-01 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`, and `BUILD SUCCESS` with all tests passing.",
